# Democracy Lens Project Commit Template
#
# Use this format for commit messages:
# <type>: <subject>
#
# Types:
#   feat:     New feature
#   fix:      Bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation changes
#   style:    Formatting, missing semicolons, etc.
#   refactor: Code restructuring without changing behavior
#   test:     Adding or updating tests
#   chore:    Maintenance tasks, dependencies, etc.
#   data:     Data updates or ETL changes
#
# Example:
#   feat: Add V-Dem democracy indices to dashboard
#   fix: Correct date parsing in Freedom House ETL
#   docs: Update deployment instructions for Neon
#   data: Update Freedom House scores through 2024
#
# Guidelines:
# - Keep subject line under 50 characters
# - Use imperative mood ("Add feature" not "Added feature")
# - Don't end subject line with a period
# - Use the body to explain what and why (not how)
# - Maintain project anonymity (no personal references)
#
# Body (optional, leave blank line after subject):


# Maintained by: Democracy Lens Project
# Contact: GitHub Issues
